<task id="051" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Outbound send path — persist-on-send + echo-dedup wiring (messaging dispatch)</title>
    <phase>W5 — BFF Endpoints</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>7</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>020,031,040,010,011</dependencies>
    <blocks>062</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication, acs</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Wires the outbound messaging send end-to-end through the BFF (authZ → channel dispatch → server-side ACS SendMessage → persist-on-send → enrichment) and MUST guarantee exactly-once persistence despite the Event Grid echo of our own message (idempotent dedupe on ACS message id). Correctness-critical concurrency/idempotency wiring across the send + inbound-capture seams; BFF-touching (publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification); code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W5</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-04</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Wire the **outbound messaging send** path, per ADR-045 rule 3 (persist-on-send) and design §4:

    `PCF send/respond accessory → BFF (authZ) → CommunicationService dispatches to the messaging ICommunicationChannelSender (task 020) → ACS SendMessage (server-side, using the sending user's server-minted token from task 010) → persist sprk_communication (type=Message, sprk_thread set via the task-040 IThreadResolver) → enrichment (association + RAG, best-effort/non-fatal)`.

    **The echo-dedup invariant is the load-bearing correctness property.** ACS emits an Event Grid `ChatMessageReceivedInThread` for our own outbound message; the inbound ingestor (task 031) dedupes on the ACS message id via `IIdempotencyService`, so the echo is a **no-op**. The seam: outbound persists on send AND records the ACS message id so the inbound capture recognizes and skips the echo — inbound stays capture-on-event, outbound stays persist-on-send, with no collision and no double-write.

    **Acceptance MUST include: sending once yields exactly one persisted `sprk_communication` record despite the echo.** Enrichment and thread assignment MUST be best-effort and MUST NOT fail the send (NFR-02). Token minting is server-side only; no ACS token or admin capability reaches the client (NFR-05); no client-side ACS SDK (NFR-04).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF architect for the Communication subsystem. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/` (send path + channel dispatch), the net-new `Services/Communication/Acs/` (identity/token/thread ops), and the inbound capture idempotency seam. Fluent in ADR-045 (channel seams / rule 3 persist-on-send), ADR-028 (server-side token minting; no `new` credential), ADR-003/ADR-008/ADR-019 (authZ seams / endpoint filters / ProblemDetails), the `IIdempotencyService` contract, NFR-02 (best-effort enrichment), NFR-03 (idempotent capture), §10 BFF Hygiene, §11 Component Justification.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Outbound messaging send is wired end-to-end: BFF authZ → `CommunicationService` dispatches by `CommunicationType.Message` to the messaging `ICommunicationChannelSender` → server-side ACS `SendMessage` with the sender's minted token → persist-on-send `sprk_communication` (thread lookup set via `IThreadResolver`) → best-effort enrichment. The Event Grid echo of our own message is a proven no-op via idempotency on the ACS message id — sending once yields exactly one persisted record. Enrichment/thread-assignment never fail the send. No ACS token or SDK reaches the client. Build clean; send + echo-dedup + best-effort tests pass; publish-size delta + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §4 resolves the synopsis's D-02 in favor of the platform's outbound pattern: persist-on-send (ADR-045 rule 3). Only inbound persists on event; both directions invoke enrichment (direction symmetry). The subtlety unique to a live-transport channel is the echo: ACS delivers our own outbound message back as an Event Grid `ChatMessageReceivedInThread`. Without dedupe, the outbound persist AND the inbound capture would both write the same message → two `sprk_communication` rows. The dedupe seam (task 031, `IIdempotencyService` keyed on the ACS message id) makes the echo a no-op — this task WIRES the outbound side of that seam: it must capture the ACS message id at send time and persist it so the inbound path recognizes the echo and skips it.

      Component Justification (§11): (1) Existing — the channel dispatch (`CommunicationChannelDispatcher`), the messaging sender (task 020), the ACS identity/token/thread ops (tasks 010/011), the `IThreadResolver` (task 040), and the idempotency service already exist; this task adds NO new service — it is wiring across existing seams. (2) Extension — extends the existing `CommunicationService` send path to dispatch the `Message` type and set the thread + ACS correlation on persist; reuses the outbound send endpoint contract. (3) Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete): without this wiring an outbound message either never reaches ACS (no live delivery to future surfaces) or double-persists on echo (FR-04 acceptance "exactly one persisted record" fails) — named contract failures, not "future flexibility."

      NFR-02 discipline: enrichment (association + RAG) and thread assignment are best-effort and MUST NOT fail the send. A send that reached ACS + persisted MUST succeed to the caller even if enrichment throws — enrichment failures are logged/deferred, never surfaced as a send failure. NFR-05/NFR-04: the ACS token is minted server-side (task 010) and used by the BFF to act as the sending participant; no token or ACS SDK reaches the browser in R1.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs (send path — dispatch Message + persist-on-send + thread set)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/ (MessagingChannelSender from task 020; CommunicationChannelDispatcher)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Acs/ (identity/token minting task 010; thread/membership ops task 011)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ (IThreadResolver task 040; IIdempotencyService echo-dedup seam task 031)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ (outbound send endpoint)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-04 / ADR-045 rule 3">Outbound: BFF authZ → messaging sender dispatch → server-side ACS SendMessage → persist-on-send `sprk_communication` (thread set) → enrichment. Persist-on-send (NOT capture-on-event for outbound).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-04 / NFR-03">Echo-dedup: the Event Grid echo of our own message is a no-op via idempotency on the ACS message id. Sending once yields EXACTLY ONE persisted record. Capture the ACS message id at send time so the inbound path (task 031) recognizes + skips the echo.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02">Enrichment + thread assignment are best-effort and MUST NOT fail the send. A send that reached ACS + persisted succeeds to the caller even if enrichment throws.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05 / ADR-028">ACS token minted server-side only; the BFF uses the sender's minted token to act as the participant; MUST NOT `new` a credential / `ConfidentialClientApplication`; inject central `TokenCredential` + canonical Dataverse interfaces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">No client-side ACS SDK; no ACS token or admin capability reaches the client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Dispatch by `CommunicationType` (`Message` = 100000004) through the existing `CommunicationChannelDispatcher`; `CommunicationService` stays Graph-free; MUST NOT fork a second send path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 / ADR-008 / ADR-019">Send endpoint carries the authorization seam + endpoint filter; errors return RFC 7807 ProblemDetails.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Thread anchor via the existing regarding family through `IThreadResolver`; MUST NOT add a second regarding mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032 / ADR-018">Registration unconditional / Null-Object for any feature-gated dependency; no asymmetric registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">§11 Component Justification: state the concrete FR-04 failure modes prevented (no delivery / double-persist). §10 bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

