    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Type-keyed channel dispatch" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/CommunicationChannelDispatcher.cs">
        `ResolveSender(Message)` returns the messaging sender; `CommunicationService` dispatches by `CommunicationType` — no dispatch-site edit per channel (email-r4 task 016 pattern).
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Persist-on-send + direction-symmetric enrichment" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs">
        Outbound persists on send and invokes enrichment; mirror the email outbound path (ADR-045 rule 3). Thread set via `IThreadResolver`.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Idempotent echo-dedup" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ (IIdempotencyService)">
        Persist the ACS message id at send time; the inbound normalizer (task 031) dedupes on that id so the Event Grid echo is a no-op — the seam that lets outbound persist-on-send coexist with inbound capture-on-event.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `CommunicationService` send path + `CommunicationChannelDispatcher` + the task-020 `MessagingChannelSender` + the task-010/011 ACS identity/token/thread ops + the task-031 `IIdempotencyService` echo-dedup contract + the task-040 `IThreadResolver` to map the exact wiring points. Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + §11.</step>
    <step order="2">Wire dispatch: `CommunicationService` resolves the messaging sender for `CommunicationType.Message` via the dispatcher (no new send path; no Graph in `CommunicationService`).</step>
    <step order="3">Wire ACS send: the messaging sender calls server-side ACS `SendMessage` using the sending user's server-minted token (task 010); capture the returned ACS message id.</step>
    <step order="4">Wire persist-on-send: persist `sprk_communication` (type=Message) with `sprk_thread` set via `IThreadResolver` (find-or-create) and the ACS message id + chat thread id recorded on the record (the correlation keys the echo-dedup uses).</step>
    <step order="5">Wire echo-dedup coordination: ensure the ACS message id is registered/persisted such that the inbound ingestor (task 031) recognizes the echo and skips re-persisting. Confirm the idempotency key contract matches on both sides.</step>
    <step order="6">Wire enrichment as best-effort/non-fatal (NFR-02): invoke after persist; a thrown enrichment/thread-assignment error is logged/deferred and MUST NOT fail the send.</step>
    <step order="7">Confirm the send endpoint carries the ADR-003/ADR-008 authorization seam + filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails; registration unconditional (ADR-032). No ACS token/SDK leaves the server (NFR-04/NFR-05).</step>
    <step order="8">Write tests: (a) send dispatches through `ResolveSender(Message)` → ACS SendMessage → one persisted `sprk_communication` (type=Message) with thread set; (b) **ECHO-DEDUP: sending once, then delivering the ACS echo event through the inbound path, yields EXACTLY ONE persisted record** (dedupe on ACS message id); (c) a duplicate echo delivery still yields one record; (d) BEST-EFFORT: an enrichment/thread-assignment exception does NOT fail the send (record still persisted, caller still succeeds); (e) NEGATIVE: no ACS token is returned to the caller (server-side only).</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm existing send tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline (ACS SDKs are thin over `Azure.Core`).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus echo-dedup exactly-once + best-effort non-fatal enrichment + no token leak); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus FR-04, ADR-045 rule 3, NFR-02/03/04/05, §11). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path; shared `Services/Communication/`; coordinate with `notification-spine-r1`).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (051 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (dedupe key/registration point, where the ACS message id is persisted, best-effort enrichment wiring).</step>
  </steps>

