  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An outbound message dispatches through `CommunicationChannelDispatcher.ResolveSender(Message)` to the messaging sender and calls server-side ACS `SendMessage` with the sender's minted token; `CommunicationService` remains Graph-free.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The message persists once as `sprk_communication` (type=Message) with `sprk_thread` set via `IThreadResolver` and the ACS message id + chat thread id recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ECHO-DEDUP: sending once and then delivering the ACS Event Grid echo through the inbound path yields EXACTLY ONE persisted record (dedupe on ACS message id).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A duplicate echo delivery still yields exactly one record (idempotent).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BEST-EFFORT: an enrichment or thread-assignment exception does NOT fail the send — the record is still persisted and the caller still succeeds (NFR-02).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: no ACS token or admin capability is returned to the caller; no client-side ACS SDK is introduced (NFR-04/NFR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Send endpoint carries the authorization seam/filter + ProblemDetails; registration is unconditional (ADR-032).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; publish-size delta reported vs ~45.30 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 020 (messaging sender), 031 (idempotent echo-dedup seam), 040 (`IThreadResolver`), 010 (server-minted token), 011 (thread/membership ops). Blocks 062 (PCF send/respond accessory drives this path). The exactly-once echo-dedup invariant is the reason this task is effort `xhigh`: hand-trace the send → ACS → echo → inbound-skip sequence and reproduce it empirically before trusting the wiring (§10 F.3 empirical-reproduction-first). The dedupe key MUST match on both the outbound-register and inbound-skip sides — a key mismatch silently double-persists.

    Coordinate on the `threadId` contract with `notification-spine-r1` (messaging is its R2 consumer) — not an R1 blocker (R1 polls), but keep the persisted correlation shape aligned.
  </notes>

